152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (My fascination for cars started when I was introduced to the modified car scene and I realized that cars can be so much  ore personal. I never viewed a car to be something like that of a favorite toy whilst also being you can grow attached to and make truely your own. There's a phrase in car culture, "Built Not Baught", referring to how car enthusiasts dont drive their cars without modifying the car or changing things entirely from the stock factory version of the car. This reeled me in because I've always been a fan of expressing and I saw cars a very fun, functional and exhilarating canvas.   )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (When it comes to the bigger picture and how I want my "EKSTAZ expression" to my lifestyle. I want to make car culture a big part of EKSTAZ's brand as it is one of the main things that sustain the type of culture and lifestyle that EKSTAZ embodies. Not only in designs and the aesthetics but also the type of people and life that fast, tuned and modified cars bring to the table.  High speeds and high minds would have been the untold motto of the brand. Cars being an integral part of the brand require me to- well- have nice cars. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (The automobile industry is also one that I would love to collaborate with. It is one of the very few markets that designers haven't tapped into with their OWN flavor, rather than making merchandise where the designers only contribution is usually just their logo somewhere on the product. Fast cars and lives with the sweet balance of stillness in the moment is what EKSTAZ will bring.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
