/T (                                                             Who holds it, the Church or Science? The lightbulb is this wisdom that both parties seem to claim to have. The effect used on the bulb is "Luminosity" which is associated to the term "Enlightened" or "Enlightenment". How life on Earth was created can be explained by either the Cell Theory or the book of Genesis. The two basic standpoints are as mentioned \(science and religion\) but the interesting and dynamic part is how man deals with the divide in both sources of wisdom and knowledge. Some try to bridge the differences while finding common ground and try to connect religion and science. )
/E (                                                             Who holds it, the Church or Science? The lightbulb is this wisdom that both parties seem to claim to have. The effect used on the bulb is "Luminosity" which is associated to the term "Enlightened" or "Enlightenment". How life on Earth was created can be explained by either the Cell Theory or the book of Genesis. The two basic standpoints are as mentioned \(science and religion\) but the interesting and dynamic part is how man deals with the divide in both sources of wisdom and knowledge. Some try to bridge the differences while finding common ground and try to connect religion and science. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 92 0 R
/T (Other try to stick to one side but eventually go off on a tangent, trying to prove the other wrong instead of proving themselves correct whilst working productively. There are also some who successfully find the balance, boundary and limit between the two and continue to work in their chosen path. I have chosen a rather aesthetic and "beautiful" image to represent a part of the universe and the hands of God and Man from "The Creation of Adam" by Michelangelo. I do this to show what lays beyond the limit to our knowledge at this point of time and the fact that when we could never go to the outer reaches of space where such a view is as real as you and me, most importantly, far enough to understand wisdom, time, physics and comprehending the vastness of space. The two versions "Of God and Man" are made regarding this divide. One where Mythology and Science fuse and illuminate the bright filament of Wisdom, but will never be able to gaze into the blinding brightness long enough. )
/E (Other try to stick to one side but eventually go off on a tangent, trying to prove the other wrong instead of proving themselves correct whilst working productively. There are also some who successfully find the balance, boundary and limit between the two and continue to work in their chosen path. I have chosen a rather aesthetic and "beautiful" image to represent a part of the universe and the hands of God and Man from "The Creation of Adam" by Michelangelo. I do this to show what lays beyond the limit to our knowledge at this point of time and the fact that when we could never go to the outer reaches of space where such a view is as real as you and me, most importantly, far enough to understand wisdom, time, physics and comprehending the vastness of space. The two versions "Of God and Man" are made regarding this divide. One where Mythology and Science fuse and illuminate the bright filament of Wisdom, but will never be able to gaze into the blinding brightness long enough. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
