/Title (JORDAN P. 'S EXPLAINATION)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 940 0 R
/Next 298 0 R
>>
endobj
620 0 obj
<<
/Title (Some of life's most important questions are answered  with the understanding of how to balance things. Knowing where to draw the line with everything is usually the most important piece of wisdom a person can have. In my 20 years of being alive I would think I grew up relatively fast, forcing myself to learn about people and the meanings of all sorts of things pretty early on in life. From a third persons perspective a life such as mine would look mundane, polished and easy going. As i grew up, met and spoke to countless more people; i started to learn how people are with problems. Everyone has their fair share of hurdles in life. Some individuals are better equipped for any specific problem than others, who in turn may be worse off with some other problems. Life gets "tough" when your combination of problems is just the type that you may not be the best at dealing with.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 298 0 R
/Next 621 0 R
>>
endobj
621 0 obj
<<
/Title (Lets take for example, a teenager with a broken family  who doesn't see the importance in his parents relationship with each other as long as they treat him well. This boy may, in turn, be horribly affected by negative thoughts about his career or friends. Another teenager exists somewhere in the world that has the right mindset and power through hurdles that show up while he builds his career but cant bear the thought of committing to other things while his family remains dysfunctional.  Now imagine this type of thing but with multiple problems in each teenagers life, although unfortunately, 4 out of 6 problems for example are ones that that specific individual cant handle. He's being hammered because he just cant balance between problems and cant balance priorities.  In my personal experience, this balance is the one between order and chaos. The Yin and Yang of life.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 298 0 R
/Prev 620 0 R
>>
endobj
